.TH WAYPINYIN 1 "2026-11-14" "Waypinyin 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
waypinyin \- offline Pinyin input method for IBus
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B waypinyin
.RI [ --settings " | " --check-data " | " --help " | " --version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Waypinyin provides Chinese Pinyin input through IBus, primarily for GNOME Wayland.
Without arguments it serves as an IBus engine. Select Waypinyin in the desktop's
input source settings after installation and a session restart.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --settings
Open input preferences and dictionary management.
.TP
.B --check-data
Load and validate the dictionary, without requiring a display or an IBus connection.
.TP
.B --help, -h
Show command help.
.TP
.B --version, -V
Show the program version.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WAYPINYIN_LEXICON
Override the dictionary image with an explicit file path. An invalid path is an error.
Only use trusted dictionary images; do not modify or truncate an image while mapped.
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Absolute user data directory. Defaults to $HOME/.local/share.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Absolute configuration directory. Defaults to $HOME/.config.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/waypinyin/config.toml
Input preferences.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/waypinyin/user.txt
Personal learning log. Contains locally stored typing choices and confirmed input-code frequency counters used for preloading.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/waypinyin/dictionaries/
User-imported dictionaries, retained on package removal.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on success; two for invalid arguments; nonzero for startup or data errors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ibus (1)
